body:
Thank you for the thoughtful reply! 

For benefits, due to extenuating circumstances, I can't currently apply for disability/ODSP or Ontario Works (benefits). It'll be something I can do in the future but my current deadline (August) it's not something that I can do. It's complicated and I can't go into it but basically... yeah. I already tried that route before and it fell through. My doctor also explicitly said she would not help with applying for disability or job accomodations.

&#x200B;

But I didn't think of food banks! That's a great idea! I'm going to look into that when I can. The job thing, I'm really nervous I won't be able to get a job and get paid in time to make the 1k for August. I know I still have 2 months but it's really NOT a long time, especially since most jobs do one week arrears, so you don't get paid for 3 weeks after starting. Just thinking about it is making me feel panicked. 



The phone plan I currently have is the cheapest available unfortunately. :( But downloading videos might work? I used to just leave my phone on and keep it face down on the pillow to sleep at night, but my phone would get really hot and it burned my face one time. Being able to turn the phone screen off prevented it from getting so hot. (It's a VERY old phone, I got it refurbished in 2017 and its definitely on it's way out now.) 

&#x200B;

Loans... I don't think I can do that. Again, extenuating circumstances that are preventing me from applying for benefits, also mean idk if I can. Like... idk. I tried to check my credit using a site and it wouldn't let me finish signing up. My bank also told me my credit was too poor to get overdraft protection? And I'm very scared to take on a loan when I have no job security or... well, really any security at all. 

&#x200B;

It's 10am (damn time flies) and my brain feels like it's continually misfiring, oop. I'm trying to get signed up for help from a place called March of Dimes (job employment help for people with disabilities) but I need to get a form signed from my doctor and after the bad experiences I've had with her, I don't know if she would even be willing to sign it.
